VERSION 0 — Academic+ (Foundation Version)
Project Name :- STACK-MARKET
Version :- 0.0
Goal
Version 0 is the academic and portfolio foundation of the STACK-MARKET ecosystem. The objective is not to create the world's smartest financial AI but to build a clean, professional, and well-structured stock market analysis and prediction application that exceeds the quality expected of a final-year engineering project.
This version demonstrates software engineering skills, machine learning knowledge, UI development, data processing, and application architecture. It should be suitable for college submission, technical interviews, internships, and as the foundation for all future versions.
The software focuses on historical stock data analysis, AI-based price prediction, technical indicators, trading simulation, and portfolio evaluation. Every component must be modular, documented, tested, and designed so that it can be extended without major rewrites in future versions.
The architecture must follow industry coding practices, including clean project organization, logging, configuration management, model persistence, exception handling, testing, and reusable modules. Although Version 0 is an academic application, every design decision should anticipate the requirements of later commercial versions.
The software will support desktop operation and provide a modern graphical user interface that enables users to download market data, train prediction models, simulate trading strategies, visualize results, and evaluate model performance. The emphasis is on correctness, maintainability, and extensibility rather than real-time intelligence.
Version 0 is considered complete when it represents an Academic+ project that is significantly above typical university standards and serves as a stable foundation for industrial development.

VERSION 1 — Industry Version
Project Name :- STACK-MARKET
Version :- 1.0
Goal
Version 1 transforms STACK-MARKET from an academic application into a real commercial product that can be released to the public. The objective is to build a reliable, secure, scalable, and user-friendly stock market intelligence platform that solves real problems faced by investors and traders.
This version introduces user accounts, cloud synchronization, secure authentication, subscriptions, watchlists, notifications, portfolio management, enhanced AI prediction models, news integration, paper trading, and cross-platform support for desktop, web, and Android. The system evolves from an offline machine learning application into an online software service.
The AI becomes significantly more capable by combining multiple forecasting approaches, technical analysis, market indicators, and news processing to generate intelligent predictions and actionable insights. The software continuously monitors market activity during trading hours, evaluates user portfolios, generates alerts, and provides explanations that help users make informed investment decisions.
Version 1 emphasizes reliability, security, usability, and software engineering excellence. The platform must be capable of supporting thousands of concurrent users while maintaining high performance, low latency, strong security, and a polished user experience.
This version marks the official public launch of STACK-MARKET and establishes its presence as a professional stock market analysis platform.

VERSION 2 — Enterprise / Market Competition Version
Project Name :- STACK-MARKET
Version :- 2.0
Goal
Version 2 elevates STACK-MARKET into an enterprise-grade financial intelligence platform capable of competing with established market leaders such as Bloomberg Terminal, TradingView, AlphaSense, Koyfin, TrendSpider, and other professional financial software.
The software evolves from providing predictions into delivering comprehensive financial intelligence. It integrates real-time market feeds, company financial statements, macroeconomic indicators, alternative datasets, global news, sector analysis, portfolio analytics, risk management, explainable AI, institutional research tools, and advanced quantitative models.
Artificial Intelligence becomes a collection of specialized systems that continuously monitor markets, classify events, estimate impact, evaluate risk, analyze company fundamentals, interpret technical indicators, summarize financial reports, and explain reasoning behind every recommendation.
The platform supports institutional workflows, enterprise dashboards, collaboration, API access, advanced screening, strategy development, portfolio optimization, backtesting, scenario analysis, and comprehensive market research.
Performance, scalability, reliability, security, and explainability become enterprise-level requirements. Every module is designed to operate continuously with high availability and professional operational standards.
Version 2 establishes STACK-MARKET as a comprehensive financial intelligence platform suitable for serious investors, analysts, researchers, financial institutions, and professional traders.

VERSION 3 — Artificial Financial Intelligence (Dream Version)
Project Name :- STACK-MARKET
Version :- 3.0
Goal
Version 3 realizes the long-term vision of STACK-MARKET as an Artificial Financial Intelligence platform. Rather than functioning as a conventional trading application or prediction system, the software becomes an intelligent financial operating system capable of continuously understanding, reasoning about, and interpreting the global financial ecosystem.
The platform maintains a continuously updated representation of the market by integrating structured financial data, company information, regulatory filings, macroeconomic events, geopolitical developments, product launches, supply chain relationships, technological advances, public announcements, historical behavior, and other relevant sources. Instead of merely reacting to information, the system continuously builds and updates its understanding of how events influence companies, industries, sectors, and financial markets.
Artificial Intelligence is implemented as a coordinated ecosystem of specialized reasoning agents. Independent AI systems monitor markets, verify information sources, evaluate credibility, classify events, analyze companies, estimate causal relationships, model economic interactions, simulate future scenarios, detect anomalies, identify opportunities, evaluate risks, and explain every conclusion through transparent reasoning.
Rather than producing a single price prediction, the platform generates multiple future scenarios with associated probabilities, confidence estimates, supporting evidence, and risk analysis. Every recommendation is accompanied by detailed explanations describing why the prediction was generated, which factors contributed most significantly, which uncertainties remain unresolved, and how new information may change future expectations.
The system continuously learns from newly available information while preserving reproducibility of historical analyses. It develops comprehensive knowledge about companies, industries, governments, markets, and their relationships without making autonomous investment decisions. Users remain fully responsible for all trading activity while the AI acts as an exceptionally capable financial intelligence assistant.
Version 3 represents the ultimate vision of STACK-MARKET: an AI-powered financial intelligence operating system that continuously observes, understands, explains, and forecasts the behavior of global financial markets to assist investors, researchers, institutions, and organizations in making better-informed decisions through transparent, evidence-based, continuously evolving intelligence.

| Version | Purpose                                       | Identity                                                 |
| ------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| **V0**  | Build a strong academic and portfolio project | Academic+ Stock Analysis & Prediction Application        |
| **V1**  | Launch a commercial product                   | Professional AI Stock Market Platform                    |
| **V2**  | Compete with established financial software   | Enterprise Financial Intelligence Platform               |
| **V3**  | Achieve the long-term vision                  | Artificial Financial Intelligence (AFI) Operating System |